The element renderer of the drake surface is definition-backed: gendrake.ElementOf (GitHub #11)

OWNING ISSUE: GitHub #11 (the generator's own text as definitions), open; it stays open. The next related point after
d06bed5. This record also carries the fold of d06bed5 into DRACO.md, the handoff and the resume prompt.

ACCEPTED by Dev on 2026-11-12: "Accepted, build it", on the recommendation that the element renderer, the last
hand-written renderer of the emitter, cross to one definition, `draco.gendrake.ElementOf`: taking an element, its level
and the name spelling as an explicit dependency `(TypeElement -> Text)`, carrying the rendered lines as `[Text]` and
recursing into parameters, bodies and case statements; `Drake.emit`'s `elementLines` checking its refusals first and
then delegating; the hand-written renderer kept as the test reference; one suite comparing the two over every element
in main and mods, its headline in the gate grep.

MEASURED before recommending: about 60 lines of renderer (leaf line, dyn block, case block, indented section), 1003 leaf
lines and 89 blocks over main and mods; the keyword (`Keyword`), the value (`ExpressionOf`) and the type (`TypeFormOf`)
already definitions, the type slot adding one rule (a top-level arrow in a pair); a method's formals on Dynamic alone,
which a definition holding a TypeElement cannot reach (ten dyns carry them). NOT probed before the recommendation, and
said so: whether a definition recursing with a function-typed parameter and returning a list generates and compiles.
The probe was the first build step.

BUILT:
- `src/main/resources/draco/gendrake/ElementOf.drake` (new): `type ElementOf`, one element `fix lines [Text]`, factory
  `par element TypeElement`, `par level Int`, `par nameText (TypeElement -> Text)`; body bindings `kind` (the name of
  the definition the element carries), `step` / `pad` / `indent`, `keyword` (the strictness word, then the kind's row
  of `Keyword.table`), `typed` / `form` / `slot` (the type through TypeFormOf, a top-level arrow in a pair), `spelled` /
  `rendered` / `valued` (the value through ExpressionOf, appended when there is one), `bare` and `leaf` (a `mon` or
  `con` carries a value only), `nested` and `section` (the recursion; a section's head one level in, its members two),
  `method` (the dyn block), `head` and `branch` (the case-branch), `block`, and `lines`. `uses` records TypeElement,
  Text, Keyword and Dracon. Its JSON is `DrakeCLI parse` of it and its Scala `GeneratorCLI generate`, stable on
  regeneration after compilation (the DRACO.md section 6 order).
- GenDrake lists ElementOf (drake, JSON, Scala: one member each).
- `Drake.scala`: `elementLines` is `refuseElement(element)` and then `ElementOf(element, level, elementNameText(_)).lines`.
  `refuseElement` walks the element and raises, before anything renders, on a kind with no keyword, invalid method
  formals, a value outside the tree language, and a block dyn or a case-branch carrying a value outside its body (the
  two messages the renderer had). `elementNameText` is the dependency: a method's name with its formals, any other
  element's as authored. The hand-written renderer STAYS as `private[draco] handElementLines` (with `leafLines`,
  `caseLines`, `sectionLines`), the reference the new suite compares against.
- `src/test/scala/draco/gendrake/ElementOfTest.scala` (new, 5 tests, the 89th suite): the leaf line by kind; the dyn
  block and the two case heads; the lines read on demand with the name asked of the dependency; the live emitter
  spelling through the definition and refusing four malformed elements; every element the sections hand the renderer
  in main and mods compared with the hand-written renderer.
- No surface moves: `DrakeCLI check` reads surface drift 0, json drift 0 over main and mods with the new emitter.

TWO SHAPE CHANGES the probe forced, both the engine's Text-slot rule quoting a value as a literal:
- `loc form Text TypeFormOf(element.valueType).value` and `loc rendered Text ExpressionOf(element.value).value` were
  generated as quoted strings (a construction followed by a member, in a Text-typed slot); each is bound as a function
  (`typed`, `spelled`) and applied, the form TypeFormOf and ExpressionOf use inside their own lambdas.
- `loc indent Text step * level` — a `*` tree in the JSON — was generated as the quoted string "step * level"; the
  repetition sits in a function (`pad`) and is applied. OBSERVED, not fixed and not filed: the generator quotes a `*`
  tree in a Text-typed slot, a defect of the String-slot rule no definition met before.
With those the definition generated and compiled, and its suite and the full run passed on their first attempt.

ONE DIFFERENCE from the hand-written renderer, on malformed input only and not reachable through the emitter: the
definition spells a kind with no row with an empty keyword and renders a block's stray value nowhere, drake having no
failure form; `elementLines` refuses such an element first. ElementOfTest pins the refusals.

LEFT OUT, as recommended: making method formals readable from a definition; removing the hand-written renderers; a
failure form for the guards.

